    "chapterTitle": "Conditional Execution",
    "topic": "Conditionals",
    "prompt": "Write a method called getGrade that accepts an integer representing a\n     student's grade in a course and returns that student's numerical course\n     grade. The grade can be between 0.0 (failing) and 4.0 (perfect). Assume\n     that scores are in the range of 0 to 100 and that grades are based on the\n     following scale:\n\n      Score   Grade\n     < 60     0.0\n     60–62    0.7\n     63       0.8\n     64       0.9\n     65       1.0\n     . . .\n     92       3.7\n     93       3.8\n     94       3.9\n     >= 95    4.0\n\n     For an added challenge, make your method throw an\n     IllegalArgumentException if the user passes a grade lower than 0 or\n     higher than 100.",
    "pdfPage": 37,
    "hasFigureReference": false,
    "solutionVariants": [
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\npublic static double getGrade(int score) {\n    if (score &lt; 0 || score &gt; 100) {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException();\n    } else if (score &gt;= 95) {\n        return 4.0;\n    } else if (score &lt; 60) {\n        return 0.0;\n    } else if (score &lt;= 62) {\n        return 0.7;\n    } else {\n        return 0.1 * (score - 55);\n    }\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "public static double getGrade(int score) {\n    if (score < 0 || score > 100) {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException();\n    } else if (score >= 95) {\n        return 4.0;\n    } else if (score < 60) {\n        return 0.0;\n    } else if (score <= 62) {\n        return 0.7;\n    } else {\n        return 0.1 * (score - 55);\n    }\n}"
      }
    ],
    "solutionText": "public static double getGrade(int score) {\n    if (score < 0 || score > 100) {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException();\n    } else if (score >= 95) {\n        return 4.0;\n    } else if (score < 60) {\n        return 0.0;\n    } else if (score <= 62) {\n        return 0.7;\n    } else {\n        return 0.1 * (score - 55);\n    }\n}",
    "pdfPageRange": "33-39"
