    "chapter": "Chapter 4",
    "chapterTitle": "Conditional Execution",
    "topic": "Conditionals",
    "prompt": "Write a method called quadrant that accepts as parameters a pair of\n     double values representing an (x, y) point and returns the quadrant\n     number for that point. Recall that quadrants are numbered as integers\n     from 1 to 4 with the upper-right quadrant numbered 1 and the\n     subsequent quadrants numbered in a counterclockwise fashion:\n\n     Notice that the quadrant is determined by whether the x and y\n     coordinates are positive or negative numbers. Return 0 if the point lies\n     on the x- or y-axis. For example, the call of quadrant(-2.3, 3.5)\n     should return 2 and the call of quadrant(4.5, -4.5) should return 4.",
    "pdfPage": 38,
    "hasFigureReference": false,
    "solutionVariants": [
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\npublic static int quadrant(double x, double y) {\n    if (x &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; y &gt; 0) {\n        return 1;\n    } else if (x &lt; 0 &amp;&amp; y &gt; 0) {\n        return 2;\n    } else if (x &lt; 0 &amp;&amp; y &lt; 0) {\n        return 3;\n    } else if (x &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; y &lt; 0) {\n        return 4;\n    } else {  // at least one equals 0\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "public static int quadrant(double x, double y) {\n    if (x > 0 && y > 0) {\n        return 1;\n    } else if (x < 0 && y > 0) {\n        return 2;\n    } else if (x < 0 && y < 0) {\n        return 3;\n    } else if (x > 0 && y < 0) {\n        return 4;\n    } else {  // at least one equals 0\n        return 0;\n    }\n}"
      }
    ],
    "solutionText": "public static int quadrant(double x, double y) {\n    if (x > 0 && y > 0) {\n        return 1;\n    } else if (x < 0 && y > 0) {\n        return 2;\n    } else if (x < 0 && y < 0) {\n        return 3;\n    } else if (x > 0 && y < 0) {\n        return 4;\n    } else {  // at least one equals 0\n        return 0;\n    }\n}",
