    "chapter": "Chapter 7",
    "chapterTitle": "Arrays",
    "topic": "Arrays",
    "prompt": "Write a method called range that returns the range of values in an array\n      of integers. The range is defined as 1 more than the difference between\n      the maximum and minimum values in the array. For example, if an array\n      called list contains the values [36, 12, 25, 19, 46, 31, 22], the\n      call of range(list) should return 35 (46 2 12 1 1). You may assume\n      that the array has at least one element.",
    "pdfPage": 55,
    "hasFigureReference": false,
    "solutionVariants": [
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\npublic static int range(int[] a) {\n    int min = 0;\n    int max = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) {\n        if (i == 0 || a[i] &lt; min) {\n            min = a[i];\n        }\n        if (i == 0 || a[i] &gt; max) {\n            max = a[i];\n        }\n    }\n    int valueRange = max - min + 1;\n    return valueRange;\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "public static int range(int[] a) {\n    int min = 0;\n    int max = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n        if (i == 0 || a[i] < min) {\n            min = a[i];\n        }\n        if (i == 0 || a[i] > max) {\n            max = a[i];\n        }\n    }\n    int valueRange = max - min + 1;\n    return valueRange;\n}"
      },
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\npublic static int range(int[] a) {\n    int min = a[0];\n    int max = a[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i &lt; a.length; i++) {\n        min = Math.min(min, a[i]);\n        max = Math.max(max, a[i]);\n    }\n    return max - min + 1;\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "public static int range(int[] a) {\n    int min = a[0];\n    int max = a[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) {\n        min = Math.min(min, a[i]);\n        max = Math.max(max, a[i]);\n    }\n    return max - min + 1;\n}"
      },
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\npublic static int range(int[] a) {\n    int[] copy = new int[a.length];\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) {\n        copy[i] = a[i];\n    }\n    Arrays.sort(copy);\n    return copy[copy.length - 1] - copy[0] + 1;\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "public static int range(int[] a) {\n    int[] copy = new int[a.length];\n    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n        copy[i] = a[i];\n    }\n    Arrays.sort(copy);\n    return copy[copy.length - 1] - copy[0] + 1;\n}"
      },
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\npublic static int range(int[] a) {\n    int range = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; a.length; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j &lt; a.length; j++) {\n            int difference = Math.abs(a[i] - a[j]) + 1;\n            if (difference &gt; range) {\n                range = difference;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return range;\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "public static int range(int[] a) {\n    int range = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < a.length; j++) {\n            int difference = Math.abs(a[i] - a[j]) + 1;\n            if (difference > range) {\n                range = difference;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return range;\n}"
      }
    ],
    "solutionText": "public static int range(int[] a) {\n    int min = 0;\n    int max = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n        if (i == 0 || a[i] < min) {\n            min = a[i];\n        }\n        if (i == 0 || a[i] > max) {\n            max = a[i];\n        }\n    }\n    int valueRange = max - min + 1;\n    return valueRange;\n}\n\npublic static int range(int[] a) {\n    int min = a[0];\n    int max = a[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) {\n        min = Math.min(min, a[i]);\n        max = Math.max(max, a[i]);\n    }\n    return max - min + 1;\n}\n\npublic static int range(int[] a) {\n    int[] copy = new int[a.length];\n    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n        copy[i] = a[i];\n    }\n    Arrays.sort(copy);\n    return copy[copy.length - 1] - copy[0] + 1;\n}\n\npublic static int range(int[] a) {\n    int range = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < a.length; j++) {\n            int difference = Math.abs(a[i] - a[j]) + 1;\n            if (difference > range) {\n                range = difference;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return range;\n}",
