    "chapterTitle": "Stacks and Queues",
    "topic": "Stacks & Queues",
    "prompt": "Write a method called compressDuplicates that accepts a stack of\n     integers as a parameter and that replaces each sequence of duplicates\n     with a pair of values: a count of the number of duplicates, followed by\n     the actual duplicated number. For example, if the stack stores [2, 2, 2,\n     2, 2,    24,   24,   24, 82, 6, 6, 6, 6, 17, 17], your method should\n     change it to store [5, 2, 3,        24, 1, 82, 4, 6, 2, 17]. This new\n     stack indicates that the original had 5 occurrences of 2 at the bottom of\n     the stack followed by 3 occurrences of 24 followed by 1 occurrence of\n     82, and so on. If the stack is empty, your method should not change it.\n     Use one queue as auxiliary storage.",
    "pdfPage": 103,
    "hasFigureReference": false,
    "solutionVariants": [
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\npublic void compressDuplicates(Stack&lt;Integer&gt; s) {\n    Queue&lt;Integer&gt; q = new LinkedList&lt;Integer&gt;();\n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop());       // s -&gt; q\n    }\n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());   // q -&gt; s, to reverse the stack order\n    }\n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {     // s -&gt; q\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    if (!q.isEmpty()) {       // q -&gt; s, replacing dupes with (count, val)\n        int last = q.remove();\n        int count = 1;\n        while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n            int next = q.remove();\n            if (next == last) {\n                count++;\n            } else {\n                s.push(count);\n                s.push(last);\n                count = 1;\n                last = next;\n            }\n        }\n        s.push(count);\n        s.push(last);\n    }\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "public void compressDuplicates(Stack<Integer> s) {\n    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<Integer>();\n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop());       // s -> q\n    }\n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());   // q -> s, to reverse the stack order\n    }\n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {     // s -> q\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    if (!q.isEmpty()) {       // q -> s, replacing dupes with (count, val)\n        int last = q.remove();\n        int count = 1;\n        while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n            int next = q.remove();\n            if (next == last) {\n                count++;\n            } else {\n                s.push(count);\n                s.push(last);\n                count = 1;\n                last = next;\n            }\n        }\n        s.push(count);\n        s.push(last);\n    }\n}"
      }
    ],
    "solutionText": "public void compressDuplicates(Stack<Integer> s) {\n    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<Integer>();\n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop());       // s -> q\n    }\n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());   // q -> s, to reverse the stack order\n    }\n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {     // s -> q\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    if (!q.isEmpty()) {       // q -> s, replacing dupes with (count, val)\n        int last = q.remove();\n        int count = 1;\n        while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n            int next = q.remove();\n            if (next == last) {\n                count++;\n            } else {\n                s.push(count);\n                s.push(last);\n                count = 1;\n                last = next;\n            }\n        }\n        s.push(count);\n        s.push(last);\n    }\n}",
