    "prompt": "Write a method stdev that computes the standard deviation of an array\n     of real numbers. The formula for computing a standard deviation s of N\n     values is the following, where xi represents each ith element and μ\n     represents the arithmetic mean (average) of all the elements:\n\n     σ=1N∑i=1N(xi−μ)2",
    "pdfPage": 129,
    "hasFigureReference": false,
    "solutionVariants": [
      {
        "html": "<pre class=\"java\">\n// compute/return the standard deviation of the doubles in the array\npublic static double stdev(double[] a) {\n    double avg = DoubleStream.of(a).average().getAsDouble();\n    return DoubleStream.of(a)\n            .map(n -&gt; Math.pow(n - avg, 2))\n            .average().getAsDouble();\n}\n</pre>",
        "text": "// compute/return the standard deviation of the doubles in the array\npublic static double stdev(double[] a) {\n    double avg = DoubleStream.of(a).average().getAsDouble();\n    return DoubleStream.of(a)\n            .map(n -> Math.pow(n - avg, 2))\n            .average().getAsDouble();\n}"
      }
    ],
